From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 74/74] PC5: the shader compiler a game starts (fxc.exe) run in the
 game's own process, as a title can't start a second one (Wine patch 0988)

Far Cry builds most of its shaders at start by running fxc.exe, its shader compiler, and reading the listing back. Every start failed on the console, and the game drew blurry, repeating textures. Wine patch 0988 does fxc's work in the game's process with d3dcompiler_47 when the start fails, and hands back a process that has already ended with fxc's exit code.
